## 4. Feature status summary

### Visible in the enabled templates

- Responsive two-column product layout.
- Variant-aware media gallery.
- Sale badge and product H1.
- Judge.me preview rating.
- Variant description fallback and product USP list.
- Custom stepped/card variant picker.
- Variant price, compare-at price, tax label, and stock indicator.
- AJAX add to cart integrated with the source theme's drawer.
- Static French payment-method image.
- Six configurable trust badges.
- Stand/size guide when detected.
- Product app-block support in the section schema.

### Implemented but currently disabled or unused

- Countdown timer.
- Three-product comparison table.
- Up to ten variant-metafield accordion blocks.
- Sticky add-to-cart markup and scripts.

### Present in code but ineffective or incomplete

- Variant descriptions and variant-metafield accordions do not update after an in-page variant change.
- Sticky add to cart receives an `.in` class while scrolling, but source CSS applies `display: none !important` to `.sticky-add-to-cart.in`; it is effectively hidden.
- Minimum/maximum quantities are loaded, but the custom fast-add path does not enforce them.
- “Pre-order” state is coded, but its availability calculation makes that state effectively unreachable.
- Product videos work in the initial server render, but the JavaScript gallery rebuild turns non-image media into preview images.
- “Hide variant-attached media” is respected initially but not when JavaScript rebuilds the gallery.

Do not silently recreate these incomplete behaviors as defects.

## 5. Detailed feature specification

### 5.1 Initial variant and page-load behavior

Initial variant:

- Use `product.selected_or_first_available_variant`.
- Shopify's `?variant=<id>` URL must select that variant on initial load.
- Initial price, compare-at price, stock state, gallery, description, and variant radios derive from that variant.

Source-only global scroll behavior:

- With no URL hash, sets `history.scrollRestoration = manual`.
- Scrolls to `(0, 0)` on `pageshow` and again after `load`.
- With a URL hash, leaves scroll behavior alone.

Migration rule: this is not a normal PDP feature. Do not add it unless explicitly requested.

### 5.2 Responsive product layout

- Mobile/tablet base layout is one column: media first, product information second.
- At `992px` and above, layout becomes two columns.
- Normal desktop split is 50% media / 50% product information.
- Between `992px` and `1199px`, split is 52% / 48%.
- Desktop product-information column has left padding.
- Source does not actually make the information column sticky.
- Main content uses the source `.container`; global CSS raises its maximum width to `1350px` at `1200px`.

Destination behavior:

- Reuse native page width, grid, breakpoints, gutters, and sticky behavior.
- Preserve the broad desktop two-column and mobile stacked composition.
- Avoid duplicate global container rules.

### 5.3 Variant-aware product media gallery

#### Data priority

For the selected variant:

1. If `variant.metafields.custom.variant_images.value` contains images, show only that list.
2. Otherwise show `product.media`.
3. When product media is used, optionally omit `media.attached_to_variant?` items if gallery setting `hide_variants` is enabled.

Initial active media:

- Prefer `selected_variant.featured_media.id`.
- Otherwise use `product.featured_media.id`.
- If that media is absent from the rendered gallery, activate the first rendered item.
- For a variant metafield image list, activate its first image.
- If no media item renders, fall back to `product.featured_image`; if that is also absent, show Shopify's image placeholder.

#### Media support in the source

- Shopify image media.
- External video media.
- Shopify-hosted video media.
- No explicit 3D model rendering.
- Images/video previews open through Fancybox using `data-fancybox=gallery`.
- Source Fancybox comes from `assets/main.js`, version 5.0.33.

Destination rule:

- Use the destination's native zoom/lightbox and media components.
- Preserve all media types it supports, especially video and 3D models.
- Do not add Fancybox if the destination has a media modal.

#### Gallery controls and styling

- Main media frame is square (`1 / 1`) with `object-fit: contain`.
- Only the active slide is displayed by the local implementation.
- Previous/next arrows wrap infinitely.
- From `750px`, show a horizontally scrollable row of square thumbnails.
- Source desktop thumbnails are about `130px × 130px`, use `object-fit: cover`, and show an active border.
- Through `768px`, hide thumbnails and show pagination dots.
- Mobile still shows previous/next arrows.
- Local code does not implement touch dragging; use native swipe behavior.
- Clicking main media opens the lightbox.

#### Image loading

- Active main image: eager/high priority.
- Other main images: lazy/low priority.
- Main responsive widths: `352, 600, 832, 1200, 1600, 1946`.
- Full lightbox request width: `2560`.
- Thumbnail widths: `90, 120, 160, 220, 416`; lazy loaded.

Use the destination's responsive-image snippet and loading strategy where better.

#### Variant changes

- A new variant with `custom.variant_images` replaces the gallery with that list and selects the first image.
- A variant without custom images restores product media and selects its featured media when possible.
- Arrows, thumbnails, dots, active state, modal, and accessibility must continue working.

Preferred implementation: use the native gallery selection API. If markup must change, use the destination section-rendering/component mechanism, not a reduced duplicate gallery built from string HTML.

### 5.4 Optional comparison table

Status: implemented, but disabled in all audited enabled templates.

- Renders below gallery in the left column.
- One feature-name column plus three comparison columns.
- Each comparison column has editable title and optional image.
- Column 1 represents the promoted product and gets light-blue highlighting.
- Supports up to eight rows; a row renders only when feature name is nonblank.
- Every row has values for columns 1, 2, and 3.
- Horizontally scrolls when needed.

Schema keys: `col1_title/image` through `col3_title/image`, `feature_1` through `feature_8`, and `col1_row_1` through `col3_row_8`.

Prefer a destination-native comparison section/block. Correct broken French accents before using source defaults.

### 5.5 Optional countdown

Status: implemented, but disabled in current enabled templates.

Settings:

- `countdown_text`: free text supporting `[month]` and `[time]`.
- `countdown_time`: ISO-style timestamp with timezone, or evergreen duration such as `15 minutes`.
- `countdown_products`: optional product list. Blank means all products.

Behavior:

- `[time]` becomes `days:hours:minutes:seconds`.
- `[month]` becomes the current month; source month names are hardcoded in English.
- Evergreen duration rounds to the next interval boundary and counts down.
- Expired fixed timer stops at `00:00:00:00`.

Prefer a native countdown block. Use locale-aware month names and decide whether evergreen state resets per visit or persists.

### 5.6 Sale/promotional badge

- Optional block, limit one.
- Displays editable `badge_text`; current value is `VENTE PRINTEMPS`.
- Source style: red background, white uppercase text, compact padding, small rounded corners.

Use the destination's native product-badge block/style when available.

### 5.7 Product title

- Optional block, limit one.
- Renders `product.title` as `<h1>`.
- Dark blue, bold, and responsive in the source.
- Ensure the destination page contains only the intended primary product H1.

### 5.8 Judge.me preview rating

- Optional block, limit one.
- Renders Judge.me preview badge for `product.id` from `product.metafields.judgeme.badge`.
- Source CSS aligns stars/review text and sizes stars around `18px` desktop / `17px` mobile.

Use the official Judge.me app block or existing review integration. Verify clicking it reaches the reviews area. Do not hardcode Judge.me if the destination store uses another provider.

### 5.9 Description and product USPs

Description priority on initial render:

1. `selected_variant.metafields.custom.variant_level_description`, via `metafield_tag`.
2. Otherwise `product.description`.
3. Nothing if both are blank.

Then optionally render a bulleted list from `product.metafields.custom.product_usps.value`.

Expected types:

- `custom.variant_level_description`: variant rich text or compatible type.
- `custom.product_usps`: product list of text values.

Source style is about `15px`, `1.7` line height, with a standard bullet list.

Source limitation: variant description does not refresh after an in-page variant change. Recommended destination behavior is to update it immediately and use product description as the per-variant fallback.

### 5.10 Custom stepped variant picker

For each `product.options_with_values` item:

- Render a circular step number starting at 1.
- Render the Shopify option name and current selected value.
- Render one radio-card per option value.
- Initially check values from `selected_or_first_available_variant`.
- Source gives the last option special styling and assumes it is the stand option for the guide.

#### Variant resolution

On radio change:

1. Read one selected value from every option position.
2. Find the variant whose complete option array exactly matches.
3. If no variant matches, source does nothing.
4. If matched, update variant selector, price, compare-at, inventory, button, gallery, and `?variant=<id>` using `replaceState`.
5. Dispatch `variant:change` and `product:variant-change` with `{ detail: { variant } }`.

Source shortcomings:

- All independent values display even when a combination is impossible.
- Sold-out values are not marked clearly.
- A radio's `data-variant-id` is unreliable for multi-option products.
- Variant description and accordion content stay stale.

Reuse the destination's native availability algorithm and selected-variant object. Preserve native deep linking, analytics, and app events.

#### Special cards: size

Source recognizes option names containing `taille` or `Size`.

Value mappings:

- `6 litres`, `6 litri`, or `6 litros` → family icon, `1-2 personnes`, `6 litres`.
- `8 litres`, `8 litri`, or `8 litros` → family icon, `2-4 personnes`, `8 litres`.
- `12 litres`, `12 litri`, or `12 litros` → family icon, `4-6 personnes`, `12 litres`.

Desktop uses three rectangular cards with icon, household label, and capacity. Selected card gets dark-blue border and pale-blue background. Mobile retains a three-card grid.

#### Special cards: filter cartridges

Source recognizes option names containing `cartouches`, `Filter`, or `Cartuchos`.

Value mappings:

- Smart carbon: `Cartouches de carbone intelligentes`, `Smart Carbon`, `Cartucce`, or `Cartuchos`.
- Fluoride version: `fluorures`, `Fluoride`, `fluoruri`, or `fluoruros`.

Presentation is circular image cards, about `85px` desktop / `75px` mobile, with thick selected border.

#### Special cards: stand

Source recognizes option names containing `stand` or `Stand`.

Value mappings:

- No stand: `Pas de support` or `No Stand`.
- Stainless: `acier inoxydable`, `Stainless`, or `Soporte`.
- Wood/teak: `teck`, `Wooden`, or `Teak`.

Presentation is circular image cards with thick selected border and pale-blue selected background. The last option gets this mobile layout whether or not it is actually the stand option.

#### Migration requirement for cards

Do not retain locale-dependent CSS IDs such as `choisissez-votre-taille-:-options`, `choisissez-vos-cartouches-:-options`, or `choisissez-votre-stand-:-options`.

Use theme-editor mappings, product/variant metafields or metaobjects, or a localized normalized mapping. Always show the actual option value as a fallback; source currently produces blank cards for unrecognized values.

### 5.11 Stand/size guide modal

#### Visibility

`show_size_guide` is true when:

- Section setting lists current product handle, one per line; or
- Setting is blank and any option name contains `stand` or `support`, case-insensitive.

If the handle list is non-empty, auto-detection is not used. Source puts the trigger only in the last option group, not necessarily the matched option.

#### Behavior

- Trigger text: `GUIDE DES TAILLES`.
- Centered white modal over dark full-screen backdrop.
- Locks body scrolling.
- Reads selected stand radio and changes title/image.
- Backdrop click and Escape close it; inside click does not.
- Source has no visible close button or complete focus management/dialog semantics.

Guide mappings:

- No stand → generic 6-size guide.
- Stainless → stainless-stand guide.
- Teak/wood → teak-stand guide.
- Unknown → no-stand guide.

Use the destination's native modal. Put trigger beside the actual stand option and include visible close control, dialog semantics, focus trap, Escape, focus restoration, and scroll lock.

### 5.12 Price, compare-at, tax, and inventory

Initial display:

- Current variant price.
- Compare-at only when greater than price.
- Hardcoded `(TTC)`.
- `En stock` or `Rupture de stock`.

Source treats a variant as in stock if `variant.available`, inventory is above zero, or policy is `continue`.

Available uses green text/blinking dot; unavailable uses red. Mobile puts price cluster left and stock right.

Use native market-aware money, translations, tax inclusion messaging, and availability/preorder policy. Do not copy source `window.formatMoney`; it hardcodes euros and can mishandle low numeric prices.

### 5.13 Optional variant-metafield accordions

Status: schema supports them, but none are configured in current enabled templates. Limit: 10.

Each block has:

- Heading.
- Optional emoji/raw HTML icon.
- Metafield namespace, default `custom`.
- Metafield key, default `specifications`.
- `hide_if_empty`.

Rendering:

- Native `<details>/<summary>`, closed initially.
- Rotating chevron.
- Value via `metafield_tag`.
- If empty and not hidden: `No information available for this variant.`

Source limitation: reads only the initial variant. Destination should update all configured accordions on variant change, translate empty text, and use a safe native icon system instead of raw HTML.

### 5.14 Main add-to-cart form

Source form:

- Posts to `routes.cart_add_url` as `multipart/form-data`.
- Contains selected variant ID and product handle.
- Contains all section `@app` blocks.
- Has no visible quantity selector; implied quantity is one.
- Disables button for unavailable variant.
- Button text changes for add, adding, added, error, sold out, and nominal preorder.
- Uses `disable-ajax` to bypass the old global handler, then installs a separate capturing AJAX handler.

Source AJAX flow:

1. Prevent submit for main/sticky forms.
2. Synchronize selected variant.
3. POST `FormData` to localized `cart/add.js`.
4. Optimistically update source drawer.
5. Fetch `cart.js`.
6. Re-render drawer items/totals.
7. Update cart count and free-shipping progress.
8. Open drawer through `body.cart-open`.
9. If drawer is disabled, use source toast.

FormData preserves app properties and selling-plan inputs. `basic-add-to-cart.liquid` also adds private property `_variant_image` so source drawer can use the first custom gallery image.

Destination implementation:

- Use native `<product-form>`/controller and native cart drawer update mechanism.
- Do not copy token-based cart HTML replacement.
- Do not create duplicate `name=id` controls.
- Preserve selling plans, line properties, file/personalization fields, loading state, analytics, and live regions.
- Show Shopify's returned error to customer.
- Prevent double submission.
- Open the configured native cart drawer after success when appropriate.

### 5.15 Minimum and maximum quantities

Global source settings:

- `settings.enable_minmax_buys`
- `settings.min_buy_qty`
- `settings.max_buy_qty`

Product overrides:

- `product.metafields.custom.min_buy_quantity`
- `product.metafields.custom.max_buy_quantity`

Source fetches `/products/<handle>?view=metafields` using `templates/product.metafields.liquid` for overrides and inventory.

Current limitation: the fast-add code updates `data-min`/`data-max` but does not enforce them; main form has no quantity input.

Use Shopify quantity rules/native quantity breaks first. Otherwise enforce effective min/max in product form, drawer, cart page, and requests with readable validation. Do not add an alternate product view for data already available in Liquid/native variant state.

### 5.16 Sticky add to cart

Status: markup/behavior exist but current source CSS hides it.

Intended contents:

- Product title on large screens.
- Selected price and compare-at.
- Quantity-one add form.
- Selling-plan hidden input when relevant.
- “100-day money-back guarantee” message, also hidden in source sticky CSS.

Intended visibility: fixed at viewport bottom after scrolling beyond half the product section, removed near footer. Actual `.sticky-add-to-cart.in { display: none !important; }` prevents display.

Treat as optional. If requested, use destination native sticky-buy feature sharing variant, availability, quantity, selling plan, price, loading, and errors with the main form.

### 5.17 Payment image

- Optional block, limit one.
- One fixed French payment banner, about `280 × 21`, centered below add to cart.

Prefer native enabled-payment SVGs or configurable image. Confirm payment methods apply to destination market; do not permanently hardcode source CDN.

### 5.18 Trust badge grid

- Optional block, limit one.
- Up to six badges, each optional image picker plus text.
- Blank custom image uses fallback.
- Configurable text/icon color.
- Icon size `24px`–`48px`, step `2px`.
- Centered three-column grid, normally two rows.
- Small bold uppercase centered text; reduced spacing on very small screens.
- Leaving badge text blank hides that badge.

Fallbacks:

1. `assets/icon-truck.png`
2. `assets/icon-tag.png`
3. `assets/icon-award.png`
4. `assets/icon-headset.png`
5. External warehouse icon below
6. External NSF icon below

Prefer native icon-with-text/trust blocks. Move external icons to destination-owned assets/Files.

### 5.19 App blocks

- Schema accepts `@app` blocks.
- Source renders every app block inside the add-to-cart form regardless of overall block position.

Preserve destination-native placement. Do not blindly put every app block inside the form; purchase-option blocks may require it, while others require normal block order. Test all installed subscription, bundle, warranty, review, and personalization blocks.

## 6. Data contract

### Variant metafields

| Namespace/key | Expected purpose | Required behavior |
|---|---|---|
| `custom.variant_images` | List of image/file references | Replaces normal gallery for that variant |
| `custom.variant_level_description` | Rich text/compatible content | Overrides product description |
| Configurable namespace/key | Variant accordion content | Up to ten configured accordions |

### Product metafields

| Namespace/key | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `custom.product_usps` | List of USP strings |
| `custom.min_buy_quantity` | Product minimum quantity |
| `custom.max_buy_quantity` | Product maximum quantity |
| `custom.product_badge_text` | Added to global product JSON for another source feature; not this visible badge |
| `judgeme.badge` | Judge.me preview HTML |
| `custom.month_sale` | Used by other templates; can feed countdown text but is not directly read here |

### Shopify fields used

- Product: `id`, `handle`, `title`, `description`, `media`, `featured_media`, `featured_image`, `options`, `options_with_values`, `variants`, `selling_plan_groups`.
- Variant: `id`, `title`, `options`, `price`, `compare_at_price`, `available`, inventory fields, `featured_media`, `featured_image`.

### Source settings/globals

- `settings.enable_minmax_buys`, `min_buy_qty`, `max_buy_qty`.
- `settings.enable_slide_cart`, `enable_ajax_cart`.
- `Shopify.routes.root`, `Shopify.formatMoney`.
- `window.money_format`, `inventory_text`, `enable_slide_cart`.

Do not assume these names exist in destination.

