## 9. Source event and selector contracts

Source emits `variant:change` and `product:variant-change`, both with:

```js
{ detail: { variant: matchingVariant } }
```

Source coupling includes:

- `#product-variants`, `#product-selectors`, `#product-add-to-cart`, `#add-to-cart`.
- `#inventory-indicator`, `.sticky-add-to-cart`.
- `.cart-icon span`, `[data-cartcount]`, `.free-shipping`.
- `#cart-template`, `#cart-slideout-contents`, `#cart-slideout-subtotal`, `body.cart-open`.
- `window.product`, `productVariants`, `customNiceVariantGalleries`, `customNiceProductMedia`.
- `window._getCart`, `_populateSlideOutCart`, `_toastAlert`.

These document source coupling; they are not interfaces to reproduce. Map to destination-native events/APIs.

## 10. Known source defects and migration decisions

Normally fix these in the destination:

1. Variant description is stale after changing variants.
2. Variant accordions are stale after changing variants.
3. Invalid option combinations remain selectable.
4. Sold-out option values are not clearly marked/disabled.
5. Preorder logic is inconsistent and effectively unreachable.
6. JavaScript money output hardcodes euros.
7. Numeric conversion can misread prices below €10.
8. Videos degrade to preview images after gallery rebuild.
9. 3D model media is not explicitly supported.
10. `hide_variants` is lost after gallery rebuild.
11. Sticky add to cart is hidden by `display: none !important`.
12. Min/max quantities are loaded but not enforced by fast add.
13. Source may create competing/duplicate variant-ID form controls.
14. Add errors are mainly logged rather than shown usefully.
15. Special-card recognition is case-sensitive and tied to exact multilingual strings.
16. Unknown option values can produce blank radio cards.
17. Size-guide trigger is attached to last option, not matched option.
18. Size-guide modal lacks visible close/focus management.
19. IDs/globals assume one product section per page.
20. Section initializes on DOM ready but not `shopify:section:load`.
21. Initial and rebuilt gallery media have unequal features.
22. Broad CSS such as `button:hover, button:focus { color: #fff; }` affects unrelated controls.
23. Multiple French strings/defaults have corrupted encoding/mojibake.
24. Source forces scroll-to-top and overrides browser restoration.
25. Countdown months and several ARIA labels are English on a French page.
26. Static payment/trust assets may not match destination market.
27. The section serializes the full product, all variants, every variant-gallery URL at three sizes, product media, and stock inline; this can make product HTML large.
28. The metafield request hardcodes `/products/` instead of consistently using locale-aware Shopify routes.
29. The size-guide modal lives inside the add-to-cart block, so a guide trigger can exist without modal markup if that block is removed.

Unless bug-for-bug reproduction is explicitly requested, preserve intended experience while fixing these through destination-native code.

## 11. Destination implementation sequence

1. Identify destination theme/version and exact product templates.
2. Audit native product section, gallery, variant picker, product form, cart drawer, modal, app blocks, and section lifecycle.
3. Map every approved feature to an existing component.
4. Confirm/add metafield definitions and types.
5. Add only missing schema settings/blocks.
6. Extend native variant state so all dependent regions update together.
7. Connect `custom.variant_images` without reducing native media support.
8. Layer special option cards over native availability logic.
9. Implement stand guide with native modal.
10. Route add through native product form/drawer.
11. Use native money, localization, availability, quantity rules, and selling plans.
12. Add optional comparison/countdown/sticky only after scope confirmation.
13. Test theme editor and storefront, retaining native no-JS behavior where supported.

## 12. Acceptance test matrix

### Variant state

- Direct URL with every valid `?variant=` ID.
- Every option selection resolves correct complete variant.
- Invalid combinations follow native behavior.
- Sold-out and continue-selling states.
- URL updates without reload.
- Price, compare-at, inventory, button, gallery, description, and accordions all represent one variant.

### Gallery

- Variant with multiple, one, and zero `custom.variant_images`.
- Transition custom-gallery → normal media → custom-gallery.
- Product image, external video, Shopify video, and 3D model if present.
- Variant featured media selection.
- Hide-variant-media consistency.
- Thumbnail, dot, arrow, swipe, modal, keyboard, and active ARIA state.
- Responsive sizing and loading priority.

### Product form/cart

- Main add with every variant.
- Rapid double click does not accidentally duplicate.
- Sold-out/API errors are shown.
- Continue-selling/preorder follows business rules.
- Cart count and native drawer update.
- Line properties and selling plans survive.
- Decide/test native variant image versus `_variant_image` property.
- Product/global quantity rules are enforced.
- Drawer changes/removals, cart page, and checkout receive correct variant/quantity.

### Content/optional blocks

- Variant description present/absent and product fallback.
- USP list present/absent.
- Accordions present/empty/hidden.
- Judge.me installed/absent.
- Countdown fixed/evergreen/expired/restricted if included.
- Comparison with blank rows/long text if included.
- Trust badge custom/fallback/blank.
- Payment block for correct market.

### Responsive/accessibility

- Test around `375px`, `768px`, `992px`, `1200px`, and wide desktop.
- Keyboard-only picker, gallery, accordion, modal, add to cart.
- Visible focus and screen-reader labels/live announcements.
- Modal focus trap/restoration.
- Reduced-motion handling for blinking/animations.
- No horizontal page overflow.

### Theme/platform integration

- Add/remove/reload section in Shopify editor.
- App blocks render in correct order/context.
- No duplicate listeners after reload.
- No globals collide with featured product/quick view.
- Products with a large variant count remain performant and use the destination theme's supported variant-data strategy.
- No console errors.
- Drawer/page/notification cart modes still work.
- Multi-currency and translated locales are correct.

